{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463506",
      "title": "Working with Dynamic Prop Values",
      "lectureOrder": 98,
      "videoOrder": 83,
      "sourceHash": "8a3d8521990fca746b283632623b5f65a33b4ad06ecdda0090205ce19f59dbcd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.644,
          "end": 3.35,
          "en": "Now of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.35,
          "end": 6.72,
          "en": "props cannot just be set to string values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.72,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "And of course, just like other HTML elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 13.34,
          "en": "you can bind them to dynamic values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.34,
          "end": 17.84,
          "en": "For example, is favorite currently works with one or zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.84,
          "end": 20.42,
          "en": "Now, since we have exactly two values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.42,
          "end": 25.06,
          "en": "it would make much more sense, that we want a Boolean here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.06,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "So that we make it clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 28.85,
          "en": "that this should be of type Boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.85,
          "end": 31.35,
          "en": "Then we can also get rid of that validator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.35,
          "end": 34.52,
          "en": "because a Boolean can only be true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.52,
          "end": 36.71,
          "en": "There are no other values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.71,
          "end": 39.27,
          "en": "The default value then could be false here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.27,
          "end": 41.603,
          "en": "So that is favorite is false by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.87,
          "end": 45,
          "en": "But now to pass false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45,
          "end": 49.81,
          "en": "we can't just set this to true or false here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.81,
          "end": 51.24,
          "en": "This is not how it works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.24,
          "end": 54.69,
          "en": "because this will always be some text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.69,
          "end": 58.3,
          "en": "Instead to use the true value type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.3,
          "end": 61.78,
          "en": "we need to bind this with v-bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.78,
          "end": 63.71,
          "en": "and that is something we can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.71,
          "end": 66.1,
          "en": "We can bind our own props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.1,
          "end": 70.49,
          "en": "just as we can bind any other HTML attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.49,
          "end": 74.48,
          "en": "And if we got a prop that needs a JavaScript value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.48,
          "end": 78.15,
          "en": "other than a string, then we need to use v-bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.15,
          "end": 82.26,
          "en": "or the shorthand of course, to pass in that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.26,
          "end": 84.67,
          "en": "You can, of course, still also execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.67,
          "end": 86.83,
          "en": "any JavaScript expression here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.83,
          "end": 89.28999999999999,
          "en": "call a method or whatever you wanna do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.28999999999999,
          "end": 93.083,
          "en": "but you can also use that to pass non string values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.35,
          "end": 98,
          "en": "But being able to bind props dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "is not just useful for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 103.12,
          "en": "It's not just useful to pass non-string values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.12,
          "end": 105.16,
          "en": "even though that is useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.16,
          "end": 107.88,
          "en": "But it's also useful to make those components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.88,
          "end": 109.81,
          "en": "a bit more dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.81,
          "end": 112.55,
          "en": "Maybe you forgot about it already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.55,
          "end": 115.78,
          "en": "but we have our friends here in NRA,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.78,
          "end": 119.16,
          "en": "inside of our App.vue file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.16,
          "end": 123.173,
          "en": "Now wouldn't it be nice if we could use v-for again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.53,
          "end": 126.81,
          "en": "but now repeat our own component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.81,
          "end": 130.77,
          "en": "and then pass in the different data for each loop iteration?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 132.95,
          "en": "Well, turns out you can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.95,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "You can use v-for, and also v-if by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 137.96,
          "en": "on your own components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.96,
          "end": 141.963,
          "en": "just as you can use it on default HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143,
          "end": 147.07999999999998,
          "en": "So here, I can loop through my friends like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.07999999999998,
          "end": 149.6,
          "en": "and now there's just one important rule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.6,
          "end": 152.78,
          "en": "You always need to add a key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.78,
          "end": 154.74,
          "en": "I talked about the key before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.74,
          "end": 158.28,
          "en": "Keys are important, when you deal with v-for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.28,
          "end": 161,
          "en": "When you use v-for on a custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161,
          "end": 163,
          "en": "adding a key is mandatory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163,
          "end": 165.72,
          "en": "So, make sure you add the key prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.72,
          "end": 168.41,
          "en": "You don't need to specify it in your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.41,
          "end": 170.97,
          "en": "Vue automatically knows what to do with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.97,
          "end": 174.56,
          "en": "Make sure you use it when you use v-for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.56,
          "end": 176.25,
          "en": "on a custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.25,
          "end": 179.09,
          "en": "And then here we can bind key dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.09,
          "end": 182.07,
          "en": "to friend.id for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.07,
          "end": 184.51,
          "en": "And now we can not just find key dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.51,
          "end": 187.36,
          "en": "but also all the other fields like name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.36,
          "end": 191.09,
          "en": "Here, we can set this equal to friend.name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.09,
          "end": 195.32,
          "en": "Phone number, we can set this equal to friend.phone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.32,
          "end": 197.74,
          "en": "because that is the field we have here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.74,
          "end": 200.52,
          "en": "where we store our dummy phone number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.52,
          "end": 203.84,
          "en": "And the same, of course, although for email address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.84,
          "end": 208.84,
          "en": "bind it's dynamically to friend.email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.89,
          "end": 212.88,
          "en": "And for the moment I'll leave is favorite as it is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.88,
          "end": 214.993,
          "en": "we'll work on that again later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.04,
          "end": 219.02,
          "en": "Now we can remove that second usage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.02,
          "end": 222.24,
          "en": "of friend contact, because now v-for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.24,
          "end": 226.47,
          "en": "will create multiple friend-contact elements on this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.47,
          "end": 228.803,
          "en": "One for every friend in France.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.18,
          "end": 233.3,
          "en": "And we're binding all prop values dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.3,
          "end": 237.54,
          "en": "to pass in the different data we have for every friend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.54,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "This of course also means, that we now can get rid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 242.74,
          "en": "of that dummy friend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.74,
          "end": 245.29,
          "en": "we're defining in friend contact.view.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.29,
          "end": 248.53,
          "en": "We don't need that anymore, because we already are receiving",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.53,
          "end": 251.88,
          "en": "all the prop data we need from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.88,
          "end": 254.88,
          "en": "And we can also change toggle favorite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.88,
          "end": 258.72,
          "en": "Since is favorite is now a Boolean by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.72,
          "end": 262.79,
          "en": "we no longer should check if it's one or zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.79,
          "end": 266.06,
          "en": "we can simplify this and set this friend is favorite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.06,
          "end": 269.2,
          "en": "equal to what it's currently not, to toggle it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.2,
          "end": 271.36,
          "en": "and set it to true if it was false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 271.36,
          "end": 273.53,
          "en": "and false if it was true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 273.53,
          "end": 276.65999999999997,
          "en": "And with all of that, if we now go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 276.65999999999997,
          "end": 279.5,
          "en": "you now see your different data still,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 279.5,
          "end": 283.423,
          "en": "but now in two components, that are created with v-for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 284.37,
          "end": 287.26,
          "en": "Now, toggle favorite is not working here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 287.26,
          "end": 290.01,
          "en": "let's see why that is the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 290.01,
          "end": 292.47,
          "en": "Yeah, because this check of course is wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.47,
          "end": 294.21,
          "en": "Since it's a Boolean, we should check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 294.21,
          "end": 296.993,
          "en": "if it's true or false like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 297.93,
          "end": 299.93,
          "en": "So, for now adjust this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 299.93,
          "end": 301.99,
          "en": "That now looks better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 301.99,
          "end": 304.2,
          "en": "Now at the moment, both are favorites,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.2,
          "end": 307.44,
          "en": "because I set is favorite to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.44,
          "end": 310.21,
          "en": "here on the friend-contact component in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.21,
          "end": 313.27,
          "en": "So, for every iteration we create a new friend-contact,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.27,
          "end": 315.96,
          "en": "but it always has is favorite set to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 315.96,
          "end": 318.483,
          "en": "But that is something we'll take care about later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 319.95,
          "end": 322.88,
          "en": "The key takeaway here, is that we can use v-for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 322.88,
          "end": 325.91,
          "en": "that we can bind those props to dynamic values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 325.91,
          "end": 330.25,
          "en": "and that now, we got a even more reusable component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 330.25,
          "end": 333.17,
          "en": "Hopefully making it clearer and clearer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 333.17,
          "end": 335.703,
          "en": "why components are that amazing.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
